{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T04:53:24.489Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"bd7dd4187970558a6c4aa1f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-14T04:53:24.489Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Test note: the first linked command variant (no fleet env var) fails in this environment only because the package worktree sits in a shared worktree farm where sibling worktrees of other fleet repos are picked up as the implicit fleet root, so the live-fleet freshness gate compares them against the committed snapshot. In a standalone CI checkout the same derivation finds no siblings and skips, which is the environment that guards the merge; the fleet-root variant (command 2/2) passes 21/21 with the live-fleet gates fully active. This is an environment-sensitivity gap in the implicit fleet-root default, not a catalog defect; reported to the orchestrator in the final summary rather than changed here."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T04:53:24.489Z"}],"before_hash":"6c016e9172758e67c8092651aea9562aaf9e3b6ede89800107d165ef9cb95e5b","after_hash":"1b45bc80433b829fdc0ab478dec19296a48afe84c77b8358ea81b80138a6eeec","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"235c508b54b94f886a3509e62dc361488ce277657354fa721e0aff8d12b75ede"}
