{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T07:03:39.289Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"bd7dd4187970558a6c4aa1f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-14T07:03:39.289Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Gates on the final state: npm release:check and bun release:check both passed 577/577 under the isolated identity (fresh HOME, no global git config), with the fleet root resolved so the live-fleet gates ran fully active; changelog:full and changelog:check both pass (this item enters the changelog when the orchestrator closes it after verification, matching the existing Unreleased-section pattern). The three intermittent failures seen during retries (catalog install acceptance spawn ENOTDIR / 300s timeout, and the 2000-item graph read over 10s) are the documented environment-load flakes tracked in pm-web-qdhx, pm-web-fhob and pm-web-hqqp; each passed on the very next run and clean main shows the same sensitivity."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T07:03:39.289Z"}],"before_hash":"e54056510a289d87bbd4cb4b5af2013c636ff2f3afe94f8717e90f83939cf05e","after_hash":"a53f37da8b18cf0788ba3a947dd36a1777492e60b6bcddfa7bd4e0886a1de921","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"044a0c537f3efcc43c0e8fa123e6a5034df4a99d885b686e9b2c1c070a1239c3"}
